Catch and handle rejections on the `previous` promise when chaining the queue tail and awaiting execution. If a previous sync request fails, its promise will reject, causing `await previous` to throw and fail all subsequent sync requests on the same connection without executing them.

```typescript
    const previous = this.syncExecutionQueue.get(connectionId) ?? Promise.resolve();
    let releaseCurrent!: () => void;
    const current = new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
      releaseCurrent = resolve;
    });
    const queueTail = previous.catch(() => {}).then(() => current);
    this.syncExecutionQueue.set(connectionId, queueTail);

    await previous.catch(() => {});
```

