If `secret` is not configured, `verificationStatus` is set to `'not-required'`. However, the duplicate check only returns success if `existing.verificationStatus === 'verified'`. This means idempotency is completely bypassed for webhooks without configured secrets, leading to duplicate processing. Consider checking for `verified` or `not-required` (or simply not `failed`).

```suggestion
        if (existing.verificationStatus === 'verified' || existing.verificationStatus === 'not-required') {
          return successResponse({
            duplicate: true,
            receiptId: existing.id,
            event: {
              provider,
              event,
              verified: true,
            },
          });
        }
```

